1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,385
This is my bedroom in Istanbul.

2
00:00:02,385 --> 00:00:07,308
RiskLens flagged the wardrobe with two
suitcases stacked on top.

3
00:00:07,308 --> 00:00:13,385
And it says what it cannot see: whether
the wardrobe is anchored to the wall is

4
00:00:13,385 --> 00:00:15,000
unknown, not assumed.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,481
In Istanbul, earthquake preparation
includes what is inside our homes.

6
00:00:21,481 --> 00:00:28,333
I built RiskLens for people like me, under
the Build for Your World theme.

7
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:35,000
You record or upload a short video of one
room and add optional context.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,033
Here is the real run, with the waiting
shortened.

9
00:00:39,033 --> 00:00:45,700
Muse Spark looks at sampled frames and
decides which objects are worth examining.

10
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:52,119
SAM 3.1 tracks each of those objects
through the whole video, so every finding

11
00:00:52,119 --> 00:00:54,918
is tied to an exact frame and box.

12
00:00:54,918 --> 00:01:01,667
Spark then reviews the marked frames and
separates what is visible from what needs

13
00:01:01,667 --> 00:01:02,407
checking.

14
00:01:02,407 --> 00:01:09,156
Here it found the bedroom wardrobe, the
suitcases on top, and a second wardrobe in

15
00:01:09,156 --> 00:01:10,144
the hallway.

16
00:01:10,144 --> 00:01:15,000
The actual time and model cost are kept in
the audit trail.

17
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:21,287
Each next step links to the FEMA E-74
section the model actually read.

18
00:01:21,287 --> 00:01:28,563
Here: film where the wardrobe meets the
wall, keep the top clear in the meantime,

19
00:01:28,563 --> 00:01:33,593
and ask a professional if anchoring cannot
be confirmed.

20
00:01:33,593 --> 00:01:39,701
If a source check fails, RiskLens
withholds actionable instructions.

21
00:01:39,701 --> 00:01:45,000
The links show what was read; they are not
expert approval.

22
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,785
You can re-film after making a change.

23
00:01:48,785 --> 00:01:55,657
But uploading the original video again
cannot prove anything changed.

24
00:01:55,657 --> 00:02:02,928
That check is a file hash, not model
perception, shown here on the public

25
00:02:02,928 --> 00:02:04,622
synthetic sample.

26
00:02:04,622 --> 00:02:10,000
Real before-and-after validation is still
future work.

27
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:16,388
We measured the pipeline on five synthetic
scenes previously used in development:

28
00:02:16,388 --> 00:02:22,697
Spark only versus Spark with SAM, repeated
runs, and negative controls with zero

29
00:02:22,697 --> 00:02:24,274
false confirmations.

30
00:02:24,274 --> 00:02:26,956
We record failures, time and cost.

31
00:02:26,956 --> 00:02:33,107
More findings do not automatically mean
better accuracy, and human correctness

32
00:02:33,107 --> 00:02:35,000
review is still pending.

33
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,753
RiskLens is a visual screening tool, not a
building inspection.

34
00:02:40,753 --> 00:02:47,511
If you would rather not film your home,
the sample report is one tap away.

35
00:02:47,511 --> 00:02:54,543
Find the evidence, understand what is
unknown, and decide what needs a closer

36
00:02:54,543 --> 00:02:55,000
look.
